ge in the forest in company with his wife and Laks mana.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.963,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-43-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2038006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dcfd2d9789148ced81c1bea9d0e42e941e1e1314161d79ac82ac11d9a388dcb6","compact":"ae1871fa31a4e220b2c09d95e4512e64f5c039a1a285e8a2c17aebd3f99a0b72","nasal":"ae1871fa31a4e220b2c09d95e4512e64f5c039a1a285e8a2c17aebd3f99a0b72"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-38-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":38,"verse":7,"english":"Despatched by you to the woods at the command of Kaikeyi, to what a plight will they, not inured to the privations of a forest-life, be reduced!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-43-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2038007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d4fdedc64d375e019d1f397eb936e38edc83b9fa2f43b418a9508985e9400c3","compact":"5e1e5ba9b2dc3b6e3392ecb31f1ffb93c57e87628af0619a081123f20349a9f1","nasal":"5e1e5ba9b2dc3b6e3392ecb31f1ffb93c57e87628af0619a081123f20349a9f1"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-38-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":38,"verse":8,"english":"And bereft of elegant apparel, how will they of tender years, exiled in this time of enjoyment, pass their lives in misery, subsisting on fruits and roots!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-43-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2038008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"caeb25f3cb861596fa1e8f62c0633561c14999f1773e476cbc3fbbe775c81cc9","compact":"664f9d66abc1a33482f9ce2a216ab5edbbe77c4715eb9e6bd4e3078fa3346ced","nasal":"f50d68440017cfde872bfcbd3227426462bb31d82de164bdb820dd20e3b4364e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-38-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":38,"verse":9,"english":"Will such a time present itself now that my grief removed and my desire attained, I shall here behold Rāghava along with his wife and brother?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.607,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-43-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2038009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f90a2926a7c201a5c40f534552482e0a1b2c3783cb3da753be7935e83193441","compact":"b5467b5e0beaed10dfbe35ca6fe909feac062cedb3339cae929f38fbbdc36fdf","nasal":"b5467b5e0beaed10dfbe35ca6fe909feac062cedb3339cae929f38fbbdc36fdf"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-38-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":38,"verse":10,"english":"When, hearing that those heroes have come, will Ayodhyā adorned with standards and garlands, attain fame, with her populace filled with joy?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-43-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2038010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3bb5b1a5a552a97c4fd2564a732923b677a1edf2b646be653776b445223c8b78","compact":"db085524ceb07308ba349d002adf46b2e0fbb1c578d79fd55f29133b34ff6d2d","nasal":"db085524ceb07308ba349d002adf46b2e0fbb1c578d79fd55f29133b34ff6d2d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-38-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":38,"verse":11,"english":"When, seeing those foremost of men returned from the forest, will the city overflow with delight, like the ocean on the occasion of a Parva?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-43-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2038011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f763cb5297a7b21a41ca5056536c5536c13d33824f43ee80f8a5bb7913cb74c0","compact":"72b3f66c9e0982b2e292263